<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<section xml:id="af-variables-expressions">
  <title>Variables, Expressions, and Evaluation</title>

  <objectives>
    <title>Learning Outcomes</title>
    <ul>
      <li><xref ref="lo-af-1" /> — Variables</li>
      <li><xref ref="lo-af-2" /> — Evaluate expressions</li>
      <li><xref ref="lo-af-3" /> — Simplify expressions</li>
    </ul>
  </objectives>

  <p>
    A <term>variable</term> is a letter used to represent a number. An <term>algebraic expression</term> combines variables, numbers, and operations.
  </p>
  <p>
    To <term>evaluate</term> an expression, substitute the given value(s) for the variable(s).
    For example, if <m>x = 3</m>: <m>2x^2 - 5x + 1 = 2(9) - 5(3) + 1 = 18 - 15 + 1 = 4</m>.
  </p>
  <p>
    To <term>simplify</term>, collect like terms (same variable, same power).
    For example: <m>3x + 5y - x + 2y = 2x + 7y</m>.
  </p>

  <exercises xml:id="exs-variables-expressions">
    <title>Exercises</title>

    <exercise xml:id="ex-evaluate-expression">
      <statement><p>Evaluate <m>3a - 2b</m> when <m>a = 4</m> and <m>b = -1</m>.</p></statement>
      <answer><p>14</p></answer>
      <solution><p><m>3(4) - 2(-1) = 12 + 2 = 14</m></p></solution>
    </exercise>

    <exercise xml:id="ex-simplify-expression">
      <statement><p>Simplify: <m>5x^2 - 3x + 2x^2 + 7x - 4</m></p></statement>
      <answer><p><m>7x^2 + 4x - 4</m></p></answer>
      <solution><p>Collect <m>x^2</m> terms: <m>5x^2 + 2x^2 = 7x^2</m>. Collect <m>x</m> terms: <m>-3x + 7x = 4x</m>. Constant: <m>-4</m>.</p></solution>
    </exercise>

  </exercises>

</section>
